r into the return of the wretched creature — a practice which is now illegal, and of which information should be given to the R.S.P.C.A. whenever detected.", "reference": "1901, Natal Agriculture Journal, page 744:"}, {"text": "“Is something amiss with the horse, Parr?” His gaze left the horse for a second as he glanced at Grace. “Yes, the horse has been figged. Now I just need to figure out who the culprit is.”", "reference": "2015, Becky Lower, The Cotillion Ball Saga, Simon and Schuster, →ISBN:"}], "synonyms": ["ginger"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/fɪɡ/", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "figs", "tags": ["plural"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "The piece of ginger root used in figging.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fig", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}